module Darklang.Cli.Docs.Enums

let content(): String =
  """# Enums

An enum defines a fixed set of cases. Each case can have zero or more fields.

## Define

An enum must have at least one case. Case names must start with an uppercase
letter and be unique within the enum.

Start each case with `|`. If a case has fields, list their types in parentheses,
separated by commas.

  type Status =
    | Pending
    | Done(count: Int64)
    | Failed(String, Int64)

You can label fields to describe what they hold. Use the same field order when constructing or matching a case.

Enum fields can contain records, other enums, or the enum itself. Enums can also
have type parameters, such as `Option<'a>`.

Enum types with the same case names, field types, and field labels in the same
order are treated as the same type, even if they have different type names.

## Construct

Write the type name followed by a dot and the case name. If the case has fields,
provide their values in parentheses. Each value must match its declared type.

  Status.Pending
  Status.Done(42)
  Status.Failed("Printer offline", 7)

The cases `Some`, `None`, `Ok`, and `Error` can be used without a type name.

## Pattern matching

Match enum cases by name. The type name is optional in patterns.
A field pattern can match a specific value or bind it to a variable. Use `_` to
match any field value without binding it.

  match status with
  | Done(0) -> "nothing completed"
  | Done(count) -> $"done: {count}"
  | Pending -> "waiting"
  | Failed(message, _) -> message

See `dark docs pattern-matching` for more examples.

## Tuple fields

In a case definition, `(String, Int64)` defines two fields, while
`(String * Int64)` defines one tuple field.
When constructing or matching a case that holds a tuple, use an extra pair of
parentheses around the tuple.

  let attempt = Some(("Printer offline", 7))
  match attempt with
  | Some((message, _)) -> message
  | None -> "no error"

## Equality

Two enum values are equal if they have the same type, the same case, and equal
field values."""
